Answer: You have two ways to do it. You can read and parse a bit of regexp in your code and match exactly like this one:

\begin{code}
(\w.+),\s(?:\w+\s?label: )*?^\S+(?=\s$)
\end{code}

and then split the 3 string variables into three variables by `.Split(',')`.

Or, if you prefer to extract only a part of the string you should simply put inside the groups the `\S+` regexp.

